      "observed_change": "The historical 16.2.14 declarations are kept, and public current-peer bridge custom properties (--mat-<companion>-*) are appended after them. icon-color also drops one blank line between rules. No historical declaration is removed or changed.",
      "decision_requested": "Should the per-companion theme/color/typography/density mixins (and the two density aggregates) append current-peer bridge custom properties to their historical output, so that a consumer calling the historical mixin also themes the current component? Or must they emit only the historical bytes, leaving the bridges to the separate bridge mixins (all-current-companion-bridges and the per-companion overrides)?",
      "alternatives": [
        "Approve appending: a narrow exact-byte deviation for these mixins.",
        "Reject: move the bridge output out of these mixins. Consumers then need to include the bridge mixins explicitly, and companion computed-style evidence must be re-run."
      ]
