      "observed_change": "Current @angular/cdk 22 cdk.high-contrast() emits @media (forced-colors: active) where 16.2.14 emitted .cdk-high-contrast-active ancestor selectors. core/legacy-core also include the current cdk.overlay() structural CSS (z-index position, touch-action, prefers-reduced-motion and backdrop selectors). badge-theme additionally carries the companion bridge append. The authentic-argument invocations of private-menu-common-item-submenu-icon (16.2.14 legacy-menu/menu.scss) and private-strong-focus-indicators-structural-styling('mat'/'mat-mdc', 16.2.14 core/_core.scss) differ only by this cdk.high-contrast form.",
      "decision_requested": "Should the owned ripple/badge/core output follow the current CDK high-contrast and overlay structure that the current CDK runtime ships? Or should owned Sass vendor the 16.2.14 high-contrast mixin and overlay CSS to reproduce the historical bytes? The class form depends on the CDK detector adding .cdk-high-contrast-active at runtime, and the historical overlay CSS would diverge from the CDK overlay runtime it styles.",
      "alternatives": [
        "Approve the current CDK output as necessary shared infrastructure.",
        "Reject: vendor the historical mixins and overlay CSS, and prove they still work with the current CDK runtime."
      ]
